// Hand-written wiki text. Keep to facts from the design; anything not yet decided is simply left out.
const NOTES={
about:"Sarivalto is set in the early 1980s, during the Cold War, on an island north of Finland. The island has been a monarchy for a few hundred years, and its latest king has just died. You play a CIA agent sent to make sure the island does not join the Soviet Union. There is no combat: each day you talk to different characters, and your choices, whose consequences stay hidden, decide which faction ends up controlling the island.",
locations:{
oilrig:"Diversified Petroleum's offshore oil rig. A pipeline links it to the company's headquarters, and boats run between the rig and West Saltwick Harbour, North Frostholm Harbour and Eastbrook Harbour. Einar works the deck by the drill tower.",
oilhq:"Headquarters of Diversified Petroleum. A pipeline runs from here out to the oil rig.",
fishing:"Frostholm, the corporate city in the north of the island, next door to Diversified Petroleum's headquarters. Glass towers and neon line its paved streets: the Petro Tower, Hotel Aurora, the Skyline Apartments, Nordbank, the Republican Party HQ, a casino, an electronics store, an arcade, the Nordmart store and Polar Burger, a fast-food restaurant, under billboards for Kelp Cola, Diversified Petroleum and Nordmart. Its harbour is North Frostholm Harbour. The Midnight Note, a jazz club with a LIVE JAZZ marquee, stands beside the arcade.",
kalanharbour:"The harbour of Frostholm: a fuel dock, the port office and rows of shipping containers under a Diversified Petroleum billboard. Boats run to West Saltwick Harbour, Eastbrook Harbour and the oil rig.",
southwest:"The road south from Kingsgrad to Hope Springs Gated Community, with a turning to the Army Barracks.",
north:"The road from Kingsgrad up to Frostholm, with a track west to Lake Ilmari. The track to Frostholm crosses the Valto River on a wooden bridge, and the river flows on west into the lake.",
lake:"Lake Ilmari, a quiet lake in the pines west of North West Road. The Valto River flows in from the east and out to the south, on its way to the beach. There is a wooden jetty with rowboats, and a path south to the beach. A travelling circus has pitched its big top and three painted caravans on the east shore: Bruno the ringmaster greets visitors at the big top, and Buttons the jester entertains by the campfire.",
bigtop_in:"Inside the circus big top: a sawdust ring with seats all round, where Meg the acrobat and Igor the strongman rehearse.",
caravan1_in:"The ringmaster's caravan, which Bruno shares with Igor the strongman: two bunks, a stove and a shelf.",
caravan2_in:"The performers' caravan, home to Meg the acrobat and Buttons the jester, who are a couple: two bunks, a rail of costumes and a mannequin.",
caravan3_in:"Madame Zora's caravan, hung with purple and gold, where she reads fortunes over a crystal ball.",
volcano:"The island's volcano, reached from the Mountains to the east. It rises in terraces, the stairs zigzagging up: from the lower slopes, stairs cut into the cliff at the east end climb to a lower ledge, stairs at its west end climb to an upper ledge, and a third stair at the upper ledge's east end climbs to the summit, where a rim runs round the smoking lava crater. In the cliff behind the lower ledge, a cave mouth leads into the Lava Tube. Steam vents hiss on every level. On the lower slopes, a path leads down from the main path to the Hot Springs Spa, a timber bathhouse with two steaming outdoor pools fed by the volcano's springs: a big hot pool and a small plunge pool, with lanterns and benches round them. It is a dead end.",
volcano_in:"The Lava Tube, through a cave mouth in the cliff behind the volcano's lower ledge: a passage of black basalt the lava once flowed down, still warm underfoot, with a pool of molten rock glowing at its far end, heaps of glassy obsidian along the walls and a crust of yellow sulphur crystals.",
spa_in:"Inside the Hot Springs Spa: a reception desk where Saga, the attendant, hands out towels, lockers and changing benches, and a big sunken bath of hot spring water, steaming under the timber roof.",
mountains:"The mountains in the north-east, on the way to the monastery. The Valto River rises here, from a spring-fed pool. A path leads west to the volcano.",
monastery:"The Orthodox Church's monastery, on a mountain top: the monastery church, the Monks' Quarters, a kitchen garden, and the abbot's house. It is the furthest place from the Royal Palace.",
monks:"Where the monks of the Mountain-Top Monastery live. The door opens into the refectory, with its long table, a scribe's desk and a bookcase; to one side is the kitchen, with the stove and pantry, and to the other the dormitory, where the brothers sleep.",
monchurch:"Inside the monastery church: rows of wooden pews either side of the aisle, icons of the saints on the walls, and a candlelit altar at the far end.",
east:"The road from Kingsgrad to the mountains and the farm.",
farm:"East Farm, a dead end off North East Road, where Hilda and Olaf work the land. Below the yard, the field is planted in rows of cabbages, potatoes, wheat and pumpkins. Beside the barn stands a second, older barn, its windows boarded and its doors padlocked; but a faint trail round its side leads to a loose board in its back wall, and to whatever is growing inside.",
palace:"The Royal Palace, home of the previous king's family. It is reached from Kingsgrad. In front of it is a formal garden: an avenue of clipped hedges between two frozen fountains, with statues, benches and flower beds. Everything else, from the chapel to the servants' quarters, is inside the palace; the servants use their own door at the left-hand end.",
town:"Kingsgrad is the island's main city and its hub: roads run from here to the north, east, south and west, and it also leads to the Royal Palace, Kelp Cola HQ and South Road, which leads to the Army Barracks and Hope Springs Gated Community. In the city are a gun shop, a supermarket, a bar, a tailor, a cinema, a book shop, a fishing shop, an estate agent, streets of houses (one of them for sale), the Kingsgrad Apartments, a way down into the sewers, and the terminus of the Kelp Cola tram line. The Civil Service Bureau, where the island's government business is done, and the police station, with the island's jail, and a doctor's office are here too, and a small park lies on the west side. South of the bottom row of houses, a newer street runs past Rosaria's pizzeria and a little fountain square.",
barracks:"The island's army barracks, reached from South Road: two barracks blocks, an armoury, officers' HQ and a guard post around a parade ground.",
colahq:"Kelp Cola's headquarters. Out front, Ville runs a newsstand and Rosa a hot dog cart for the office workers. The Kelp Cola tram line runs along the bottom of its grounds, between Kingsgrad and the tram stop next door.",
tramstop:"A stop on the Kelp Cola tram line, which runs in a loop from Kingsgrad past the company's headquarters to this stop, the cola factory and Eastbrook, then back to Kingsgrad along South East Road. Here there is a platform and shelter beside the track, under the overhead wire. A trail leads south into the Pine Forest.",
forest:"An autumn forest of turning trees and pines south of the tram stop, with a pond, a campfire and a woodpile in a clearing. A track leads out of its east side to the Mill, the lumber mill on the way to Eastbrook, and a track runs south to South East Road.",
colafactory:"Kelp Cola's factory, with a warehouse, a stop on the Kelp Cola tram line, and Pirkko's fast-food van parked outside for the factory workers. It is next to Eastbrook.",
millroad:"The Mill, on the dirt track between the Pine Forest and Eastbrook: the Eastbrook Lumber Company's mill, with logs from the forest stacked in its yard and stumps where trees have been felled. Ilse loads the logs.",
mill_in:"Inside the lumber mill: a circular saw over a conveyor that carries the logs through, stacks of sawn timber, sacks of sawdust, lockers, and the foreman's desk, where Bjarne keeps the books. Knut runs the saw.",
kcmuseum_in:"The Kelp Cola Museum, the company's own history of itself: shelves of vintage bottles and bottle caps, old crates, a mannequin in an early delivery uniform and the company's first bottling line, still running. At the back is the gift shop, where Wilma, the curator, sells souvenirs and postcards. Out on the street, Kelpy the cup, the museum's mascot, waves visitors in.",
clothes_in:"Flannel and Folk, Eastbrook's vintage clothes shop: rails of flannel shirts, wool coats and knitwear, mannequins in the window, and a counter where Juniper, the owner, rings up sales.",
records_in:"Vinyl Resting Place, Eastbrook's record shop: shelves and crates of second-hand records, a listening desk with a turntable, and a counter where Ruby, the owner, plays whatever she likes.",
second:"Eastbrook, the island's second town: an old timber town that has gone hip. It has its own harbour, Eastbrook Harbour, a stop on the Kelp Cola tram line, and a track that leads west to the Mill, the lumber mill, and on to the Pine Forest. Its brick streets are lined with timber houses painted mustard, slate blue, teal and oxblood, with porches, window boxes, string lights and hand-painted signs full of puns. Upper Street has the Timber Lofts apartment block, Pirkko's house, the Kelp Cola Museum and its gift shop, Henrik's and Nora's houses and the Community Centre. On the main street are the Cedar Grill, the Slow Drip coffee roasters, Vinyl Resting Place, a record shop with a mural painted across its front, the Ink and Pine tattoo shop, Flannel and Folk, a vintage clothes shop, the Eastbrook Gazette and the Timberline Tavern. Between the main street and Tram Street are a brick-paved food-cart plaza, where Dex runs a hot dog cart, and a little park with a KEEP EASTBROOK WEIRD sign. Alder Lane runs down the middle of town to the tram platform.",
savilaharbour:"The harbour of Eastbrook: a timber customs house and a warehouse on the quay, a long pier out to the boat berths, a jetty where the fishing boats tie up, and, on a rocky spit to the north-east at the end of the pier, a red-and-white lighthouse whose beam sweeps the water at night. Boats run to West Saltwick Harbour, North Frostholm Harbour and the oil rig.",
pizzeria_in:"Rosaria's pizzeria in Kingsgrad: a wood-fired oven, a counter, a shelf of wine and red-checked tables in front. Behind a door at the back is a shady back room with a card table, a safe, crates and a desk of ledgers: the pizzeria is a front for the Crime Syndicate, and this is where it counts its money. The Syndicate plays Texas hold'em at the card table in the back room, for $1 and $2 blinds, and will deal you in. Beside the counter a door leads through to the kitchen, where the dough is made.",
oldbarn_in:"Inside East Farm's old barn, reached only through a loose board at the back: someone is growing cannabis here, in four hydroponic grow beds under hanging grow lamps, fed from a water tank and drums of nutrients, with a fan to keep the air moving and a cot for whoever tends it.",
derrick_in:"The drill floor inside the oil rig's drill tower, reached by a steel door from the deck: dark steel plating slick with puddles of crude, the rotary table with the drill pipe going down through it, a mud pump, the drawworks winch, a generator thudding away, the driller's console and a rack of drill pipe.",
lighthouse_in:"The keeper's room at the foot of the lighthouse, where Signe lives and works: a bed, a table, a stove, tide charts, cans of lamp oil, and the spiral stair up to the lamp.",
lighthouse_top:"The lamp room at the top of the lighthouse, up the spiral stair from the keeper's room: the great lamp burning inside its beehive of glass prisms, windows all round, and cans of lamp oil for the night.",
south:"The road between Kingsgrad and Eastbrook. The Kelp Cola tram line runs alongside it, and a track leads north into the forest.",
west:"The road from Kingsgrad west to Saltwick and the beach.",
beach:"The beach, between South West Road and Saltwick, where the Valto River runs into the sea. The path south crosses it on a small bridge.",
village:"Saltwick, the island's fishing village, is home to the Communist Party's headquarters, a fish processing plant, a fish shop, a tired newsstand on the main street, a bar, an apartment block and houses for the fishermen and fishmongers. The village is run down: peeling paint, boarded-up windows, patched roofs, broken cobbles, slush and junk. Down a path off the main street stands Harbour Outfitters, the village's clothes shop.",
harbour:"West Saltwick Harbour, the working harbour of Saltwick, with fishing boats, a pile of fish, an old upturned hull and the fishermen Tom, Sam and Mike. Boats run to North Frostholm Harbour, Eastbrook Harbour and the oil rig.",
radio:"A radio tower reached from Saltwick. Cables run from the mast to the transmitter hut beside it, which houses the island's radio studio. Hekki's shack stands nearby.",
gated:"Hope Springs Gated Community, reached from Kingsgrad along South Road. The island's richest live here: Gustavo, the Crime Syndicate's Don, and Phil and Dario, who run Kelp Cola and Diversified Petroleum, each have a villa. It is immaculate: swept flagstone paths behind gate pillars, clipped hedges, ornate lamps, flower beds, topiary, statues and a fountain between the villas, formal gardens either side, and the Hope Springs Residences, an apartment block for the wealthy. It has paths to South Private Harbour and the Private Beach.",
privbeach:"The beach belonging to Hope Springs Gated Community, with sun loungers and a boardwalk lit by ornate lamps.",
privharbour:"The harbour belonging to Hope Springs Gated Community. No boats run to or from it: it can only be reached on foot from the gated community.",
plant:"The fish processing plant where the fishmongers Bob and Kate work.",
hq:"The Communist Party's headquarters on Saltwick's main street: two desks, a long meeting table, and cabinets of files and party archives. Anna, the party's leader, works at one desk and Helen, who leads the Union, at the other.",
apartments:"The village's apartment block: three floors of five flats each, joined by stairs from the corridor. The communists Anna, Mike and Helen live here, along with Kaisa the radio DJ, Olga from the fish shop and Gunnar from the harbour warehouse, Sirpa and Tiina, who are out of work, and the Crime Syndicate's Lucia.",
bar:"The village's bar. The bartender, Ray, lives in the flat above. In the evenings Sirpa and Tiina, out of work, sit at its tables.",
barflat:"The flat above the bar, where Ray lives.",
fishshop:"The village's fish shop, selling fresh and smoked fish.",
outfitters_in:"Harbour Outfitters, Saltwick's clothes shop for the boats and the cold: oilskins and sou'westers, cable-knit jumpers, pea coats, dungarees, wellies and watch caps, on rails along blue-panelled walls under a chart of the island. Helmi runs it.",
skyapts:"Skyline Apartments, a slim glass tower in Frostholm: four floors of five modern flats above a lobby with a reception desk. Nils, Birgit, Sanna, Greta, Ruth, Agnes, Sven, Ole, Britta, Margit and Magnus live here, and so do the Crime Syndicate's Nico. Arto and Raili, who are out of work, live here too.",
eblofts:"The Timber Lofts, Eastbrook's apartment block among the fir trees: four floors of five brick-walled flats with wooden floors, bookcases and record shelves. Maya, Jonna, Erik, Linnea, Arvid, Liv and Tor live here, with Dex from the hot dog cart, Wilma from the Kelp Cola Museum, Juniper from the clothes shop, Ruby from the record shop, the mill crew Bjarne, Knut and Ilse, the Crime Syndicate's Paolo, Jaana, who spends her days inside Kelpy the cup, and Veikko and Hely, who are out of work.",
hsresid:"Hope Springs Residences, a block of luxury flats in the gated community: two floors of five flats, with fireplaces, portraits and a concierge desk in the lobby. Colonel Halvorsen, the army's commander, lives here, as do Harald and Carlo, two of the candidates for the Republican Party's leadership, and the Crime Syndicate's Paola.",
repubhq:"The Republican Party's headquarters in Frostholm, where the party is choosing a new leader. Margit, the party secretary, runs the election from the podium beside the ballot box. Each candidate has a campaign desk: Carlo for the Crime Syndicate, Harald for Kelp Cola and Magnus for Diversified Petroleum, though the two company men's desks are usually empty, since both campaign from their companies' headquarters.",
kgapts:"Kingsgrad Apartments, an ordinary city block behind the Civil Service Bureau: four floors of five flats each. Toni, Otto, Sergeant Hanna, Doctor Lind, Rosa, Ville, Bertil, Elin and Mats, Kurt, Petra, Aino and Saga live here, and so do Eila and Marjut, who are out of work.",
electro:"Frostholm's electronics store, run by Nils: a wall of televisions, shelves of hi-fi gear and boxes stacked by the counter.",
arcadein:"Frostholm's arcade: rows of glowing game cabinets under a pink neon sign. Toni hands out change at the counter. Its machines play Snake, Brick Breaker and Invaders, at a dollar a game.",
mart:"Nordmart, Frostholm's big store, open late: fridges and aisles of shelves. Birgit runs it from the checkout.",
cinemain:"Kingsgrad's cinema: rows of red seats, a snack shelf, and the ticket counter where Otto works. Now showing: STORMWING, an action picture about two fighter pilots over the frozen North; a ticket is $4 from Otto, or take a seat.",
cafe:"Eastbrook's coffee roaster, run by Maya: a roaster by the brick wall, a counter, and a couple of tables. Behind the counter a door leads back to a small kitchen where the buns are baked.",
tavern:"The Timberline Tavern, Eastbrook's bar: a long bar backed by bottles, a fireplace, a dartboard and tables. Linnea tends the bar. In the evenings Veikko and Hely, out of work, sit at its tables. Behind the bar a door leads back to the kitchen, where the tavern's meals are cooked.",
cedargrill:"The Cedar Grill, Eastbrook's restaurant: an open kitchen behind the counter, where Arvid cooks, and tables on a rug under the brick walls. Behind the counter a door leads back to the kitchen, with its stove, oven, fridge, sink and pantry shelves.",
tattoo:"Eastbrook's tattoo shop, where Jonna works: two tattoo benches, shelves of inks, and walls covered in flash designs.",
police:"Kingsgrad Police Station. Behind the front desk, where Sergeant Hanna works, a corridor runs past three barred cells: the island's jail. The middle cell holds Mario, a bookie for the Crime Syndicate.",
commcentre:"Eastbrook's Community Centre, the Democratic Party's base: a meeting hall with a long table under the party's blue banners, where Erik, the party's leader, holds meetings.",
house_tom:"The home of the fisherman Tom.",house_sam:"The home of the fisherman Sam.",
house_bob:"Bob's old house in Saltwick, empty since he moved into the village's apartment block with Helen and now up for sale through the estate agent in Kingsgrad. A few boxes are all that is left inside.",
house_forsale_eb:"An empty timber house at the east end of Upper Street in Eastbrook, for sale through the estate agent in Kingsgrad. Only a few boxes are left inside.",
house_forsale_fh:"A slim modern townhouse in Frostholm, in the corner below the Republican Party HQ, for sale through the estate agent in Kingsgrad. It is empty but for a few boxes.",
villa_forsale:"An empty villa in Hope Springs Gated Community, in the garden corner below the Residences, for sale through the estate agent in Kingsgrad. Its fireplace is cold and its rooms hold nothing but boxes.",house_kate:"The home of Kate, the fishmonger. She lives here on her own since Bob moved into the apartment block with Helen.",
tram:"Inside the Kelp Cola tram: rows of red seats under the windows and a route map at the front. Choose a stop from the route map to ride there, or step back out of the door to get off where you got on.",
burgerbar:"Polar Burger, Frostholm's fast-food restaurant: a grill and fryer behind a long counter, a menu board on the wall and a couple of tables. Behind the counter a door leads back to the kitchen, with its stoves, fridge, sink and pantry shelves.",
newsroom:"The office of the Eastbrook Gazette, the town's newspaper. The reporter Nora works at the desks by the door; the editor, Henrik, sits at the back beside the paper's archive and files. A cast-iron printing press stands by the door, its flywheel turning, with bundles of fresh papers stacked either side.",
house_henrik:"The home of Henrik, editor of the Eastbrook Gazette.",house_nora:"The home of Nora, a reporter on the Eastbrook Gazette.",
house_pekka:"Pirkko's house in Eastbrook. She runs the fast-food van outside the Kelp Cola factory.",
palacehall:"The Grand Hall, just inside the palace doors. Doors lead from it to the Royal Apartments, the Throne Room and the Royal Library at the back, the Dining Room on the left and the Royal Chapel on the right.",
throne:"The palace's throne room, where the late king's throne stands empty on a red and gold carpet under royal banners.",
royalrooms:"The royal family's private apartments: bedrooms for Prince Leopold, his brother Augustus and his sister Daphne, off a shared corridor.",
dining:"The palace dining room, with a long table laid for the royal family. A door at the back leads to the kitchen.",
kitchen:"The palace kitchen, with two stoves, a pantry and a big table. Doors lead to the dining room and the servants' quarters, and stairs go down to the wine cellar.",
winecellar:"The palace wine cellar, under the kitchen: racks of bottles and rows of barrels.",
library:"The royal library: rows of bookcases and a reading table. One of the bookcases is a secret door to the royal vault.",
vault:"The royal vault, hidden behind a bookcase in the library: gold bars, treasure chests and the crown jewels in a glass case.",
chapel:"The royal family's private chapel, off the Grand Hall: rows of pews facing a candlelit altar, with portraits of past kings on the walls. Stairs at the back lead down to the crypt.",
crypt:"The royal crypt under the palace chapel, where the island's kings and queens are buried. The late king's tomb, under a purple pall and a gold crown, stands at the far end.",
servants:"The servants' quarters, off the palace kitchen and with their own entrance at the left-hand end of the palace front, where the royal household's staff live: a row of beds, a stove, a long dining table and the laundry.",
kchq2:"Phil's office on the second floor of Kelp Cola's headquarters, up the stairs from the reception floor: a green-carpeted, wood-panelled room with his executive desk, a portrait on the wall, a bookcase, a drinks cabinet, a shelf of the company's trophies and a table for guests.",
villa_phil:"Phil's villa in Hope Springs. Phil runs Kelp Cola.",
villa_dario:"Dario's villa in Hope Springs. Dario runs Diversified Petroleum.",
doctor:"Kingsgrad's doctor's office, below the police station: a reception desk and waiting chairs by the door, and the consulting room, with its examination bed and medicine cabinet, where Doctor Lind sees patients.",
hotel_lobby:"The lobby of Hotel Aurora in Frostholm: a reception desk under the key rack, where Greta checks guests in, a few armchairs, and stairs up to the rooms.",
hotel_floor:"The guest rooms upstairs at Hotel Aurora. The room on the right is Yuri's: alongside the bed it holds radio equipment, monitor screens and a tape recorder, much like your own set-up in the Hidden Radio Room.",
crewq:"Where the oil rig's crew sleep between shifts: a row of bunks, lockers, a stove and a table for meals. Lars and Einar bunk here.",
dphq_in:"Inside Diversified Petroleum's headquarters: a reception desk in front of a bank of monitor screens, offices along both walls, and a meeting table under maps of the drilling sites. Magnus, a Diversified Petroleum executive and the company's candidate for leader of the Republican Party, works at the desk in the corner office.",
depot_in:"Diversified Petroleum's depot: racks of pipe, stacks of oil drums and a workbench.",
petro_in:"The ground floor of the Petro Tower, Diversified Petroleum's office block in Frostholm: a reception desk, waiting seats and rows of office desks.",
bank_in:"Nordbank's banking hall in Frostholm: a long counter, the safe behind it, waiting seats, and a desk for loans.",
farmhouse_in:"The farmhouse at East Farm: a bed, a big kitchen table by the stove, and sacks of grain and potatoes.",
barn_in:"East Farm's barn: hay bales, sacks of feed and a workbench.",
civil_in:"The Civil Service Bureau in Kingsgrad: clerks' desks and rows of filing cabinets behind a long service counter, and benches where the public wait their turn.",
kchq_in:"Inside Kelp Cola's headquarters: a reception desk, a fridge stocked with the company's cola, offices, and the boardroom table where Phil holds meetings. The walls are hung with old Kelp Cola adverts (bottles, Kelpy the cup, sunbursts and seaside scenes), and glass cases by the back wall and in the lobby show off the company's bottles through the years, beside a stack of Kelp Cola crates. Stairs at the back lead up to Phil's own office, which has a couple of the old adverts too. Harald, a Kelp Cola executive and the company's candidate for leader of the Republican Party, works at the desk in the corner office.",
kcfac_in:"The Kelp Cola factory floor: a bottling line running the length of the hall, a packing bench and stacks of crates ready to ship. Kurt, the foreman, keeps watch over it, and Aino works the bottling line.",
kcwhs_in:"Kelp Cola's warehouse, stacked with crates of cola.",
whs_in:"The warehouse at West Saltwick Harbour, as run down as the rest of the village: crates of fish on ice, piles of nets and junk.",
barrA_in:"Barracks Block A: the soldiers' dormitory, with rows of bunks and lockers.",
barrB_in:"Barracks Block B: the mess hall, with the kitchen behind a serving counter and long tables for the soldiers.",
gp_in:"The guard post at the barracks gate: a desk, a radio and a stove to keep the sentry warm.",
arm_in:"The barracks armoury: racks of rifles along the walls, crates of ammunition, and the counter where weapons are signed out.",
offhq_in:"The officers' headquarters: a map table for planning, radio equipment, and the officers' desks under maps of the island.",
fuel_in:"The fuel dock's office at North Frostholm Harbour: drums of fuel and a counter where boat crews pay.",
port_in:"The port office at North Frostholm Harbour, which logs every boat in and out: a counter, desks, files and a ship-to-shore radio.",
customs_in:"The customs shed at Eastbrook Harbour: an inspection counter, files and a pile of seized goods.",
ebwhs_in:"The timber warehouse at Eastbrook Harbour: stacked lumber, crab pots, nets and a workbench.",
apartments2:"The second floor of Saltwick's apartment block, with five more flats.",
skyapts2:"The second floor of the Skyline Apartments, with five more flats.",
eblofts2:"The second floor of the Timber Lofts, with five more flats.",
kgapts2:"The second floor of the Kingsgrad Apartments, with five more flats.",
apartments3:"The third floor of the Apartment Block, with five more flats.",
skyapts3:"The third floor of the Skyline Apartments, with five more flats.",
skyapts4:"The fourth floor of the Skyline Apartments, with five more flats.",
eblofts3:"The third floor of the Timber Lofts, with five more flats.",
eblofts4:"The fourth floor of the Timber Lofts, with five more flats.",
kgapts3:"The third floor of the Kingsgrad Apartments, with five more flats.",
kgapts4:"The fourth floor of the Kingsgrad Apartments, with five more flats.",
hsresid2:"The second floor of the Hope Springs Residences, with five more flats.",
jazz_in:"The Midnight Note, Frostholm's jazz club: a dim, blue-carpeted room with a bar of bottles on one side, a stage and grand piano at the back where Leo plays the saxophone and Rita sings, and candlelit tables. Sid, who owns it, tends the bar. In the evenings Arto and Raili, out of work, sit at its tables.",
villa_gustavo:"Gustavo's villa in Hope Springs. Gustavo is the Don of the Crime Syndicate.",
clubroom:"The Club, Hope Springs' private members' club: a bar of fine bottles along the back wall, card tables for the members, and, by the fire, the table where Gustavo, the Don of the Crime Syndicate, holds court.",
house_thyme:"The house of Father Thyme, the abbot, in the grounds of the Mountain-Top Monastery.",
shack_hekki:"A shack near the Radio Tower where Hekki, an informant for the CIA, lives and listens in. Its radio set is the only way to reach Chuck, your CIA handler, who is not on the island. One of its bookcases is a secret door to a hidden radio room.",
hekki_room:"A secret room behind a bookcase in Hekki's shack, packed with radio equipment, tape recorders and banks of monitor screens. Hekki uses it to listen in on the island. Through a doorway in a partition at the back is where you, the CIA agent, live, hidden from the island, and where the game starts: a bed, a stove, a table, and shelves of supplies and tinned food. A tear-off calendar above the bed shows the date: the game runs through the 30 days of September, and sleeping in the bed moves on to the next morning. Maps of the island hang on the walls; look at one to see the whole island and where you are. On the back wall hangs a big screen with a camera on top, for video calls to CIA headquarters. In the living space a tall wardrobe holds your clothes. On the desktop PC in the radio room runs the Faction Tracker, which keeps score of how each faction stands.",
langley:"CIA Headquarters at Langley, Virginia, where the story begins, far from the island and reached only from the Jump to list. The Agency's seal is set into the granite floor of the lobby; on the wall above, the Memorial Wall's rows of carved stars stand between two flags, with the Book of Honor lying open in its case beneath them. A statue stands to one side, and stairs beside the security desk lead up to the offices.",
langley_office:"An office upstairs at CIA Headquarters, where you are briefed before leaving for the island: a broad desk, files and a safe, a meeting table, a leather sofa, the Agency's seal, a portrait and a map of the Baltic on the wall.",
transhut:"The transmitter hut at the foot of the Radio Tower. Besides the transmitter it holds the island's radio studio: a mixing desk, a microphone table, tape recorders and shelves of records, under an ON AIR sign.",
tent_pat:"Pat's camp on the beach: a tent, a bedroll and a camp stove, next to the campfire.",
gunshop:"Kingsgrad's gun shop, run by Frank: a rack of rifles, a counter and crates of ammunition.",
supermarket:"Kingsgrad's supermarket, where Lisa works the checkout: aisles of shelves and a wall of fridges.",
citybar:"The City Bar in Kingsgrad, where Eddie tends the bar. In the evenings Eila and Marjut, out of work, sit at its tables.",
tailor:"Grace's tailor's shop in Kingsgrad, with rolls of cloth, a clothes rail and mannequins.",
casino:"Frostholm's casino, with slot machines, card tables and a roulette wheel. Vince works the cashier's desk. You can play the slot machines and the blackjack tables with your own money. One of its card tables is for poker: Texas hold'em at $2 and $4.",
bookshop:"Mary's book shop in Kingsgrad.",
fishingshop:"Jack's fishing shop in Kingsgrad, selling rods, tackle, nets and bait.",
estateagent:"The estate agent's office in Kingsgrad, where Sally works. It has an empty home for sale in every town: the house a few doors along in Kingsgrad, Bob's old house in Saltwick, a timber house in Eastbrook, a townhouse in Frostholm and a villa in Hope Springs.",
sewers:"The sewers under Kingsgrad, reached through a manhole in the street (stand on it and press E to climb down): brick tunnels either side of a channel of dirty water.",
house_frank:"The home of Frank, who runs the gun shop.",house_lisa:"The home of Lisa, who works at the supermarket.",house_eddie:"The home of Eddie, the bartender at the City Bar.",
house_grace:"The home of Grace, the tailor.",house_vince:"The home of Vince, who works at the casino.",house_mary:"The home of Mary, who runs the book shop.",
house_jack:"The home of Jack, who runs the fishing shop.",house_sally:"The home of Sally, the estate agent.",
house_forsale:"An empty house in Kingsgrad, for sale through the estate agent. Only a few boxes are left inside."},
factions:{
communist:"The Communist Party wants Sarivalto to join the Soviet Union, as a Soviet republic, and to hand the island to the people who work it. It is based in Saltwick, where its headquarters stands, and is led by Anna from her flat in the village's apartment block. Three party members live in the village's apartment block, and two more, Sam and Kate, have their own houses. Across the island in Eastbrook, where most people back the Democrats, Liv and Tor from Eastbrook Harbour are party members too. Its link to Moscow is Yuri, a KGB agent working undercover from a room at Hotel Aurora in Frostholm.",
democrat:"The Democratic Party is based at the Community Centre in Eastbrook, the island's second town. Its leader is Erik. Most of Eastbrook backs the party: Maya at the coffee roaster, Jonna at the tattoo shop, Dex with his hot dog cart, Ruby at the record shop, and Bjarne, Knut and Ilse from the lumber mill are all members.",
royal:"The family of the previous king, whose death starts the story. Their seat is the Royal Palace. Not everyone in Democratic Eastbrook wants the monarchy gone: Linnea, the bartender at the Timberline Tavern, and Arvid, the chef at the Cedar Grill, are royalists. The family is divided: Leopold is the heir, but his brother Augustus, a devout churchman, has the backing of the monastery to be crowned instead.",
cola:"Kelp Cola has its headquarters in Kingsgrad's neighbourhood and a factory nearby, joined by the Kelp Cola tram line, which loops from Kingsgrad to the tram stop, the factory and Eastbrook and back. Stand on a platform and press E to call the tram. In Eastbrook it runs the Kelp Cola Museum, a polished history of the company with a gift shop, where Wilma is the curator.",
oil:"Diversified Petroleum is an oil drilling company with its headquarters on the coast and an offshore rig linked to it by a pipeline.",
syndicate:"The Crime Syndicate is run by its Don, Gustavo, who lives in a villa in Hope Springs Gated Community and holds court in The Club there. It keeps one of its people working each town: Nico and Mario, bookies in Frostholm and Kingsgrad, Paolo, a bookie in Eastbrook, and Lucia and Paola, enforcers in Saltwick and Hope Springs. Carlo is its candidate for leader of the Republican Party. In Kingsgrad it runs a front, Rosaria's pizzeria, whose back room is where the Syndicate's money is counted.",
kgb:"The Soviet Union's intelligence agency. Its only agent on the island is Yuri, who works undercover from a room at Hotel Aurora in Frostholm and acts as the Communist Party's link to Moscow.",
union:"The Union is the island's trade union, led by Helen from her flat in Saltwick's apartment block. Most of the workers at the Kelp Cola factory, in the fishing trade and at the lumber mill belong to it: Petra from the cola warehouse, Aino from the factory's bottling line, Bob and Kate from the fish processing plant, the fishermen Tom, Sam and Mike, Gunnar from the harbour warehouse, and Knut and Ilse from the mill. The foremen, Kurt at the factory and Bjarne at the mill, are not members. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
republican:"The Republican Party is based at its headquarters in Frostholm. It has no leader, and the island's two big companies and the Crime Syndicate are each trying to get their own candidate voted in: Harald for Kelp Cola, Magnus for Diversified Petroleum and Carlo for the Syndicate. Margit, the party secretary, runs the election. Its members include Nils, who runs Frostholm's electronics store, and in Kingsgrad Otto, the manager of the cinema, Frank from the gun shop, Jack from the fishing shop and the town's doctor, Doctor Lind.",
circus:"A travelling circus that has pitched its big top and caravans on the shore of Lake Ilmari. Bruno the ringmaster runs it; his performers are Meg the acrobat, Igor the strongman and Buttons the jester, and Madame Zora tells fortunes in her caravan. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
farmers:"The island's farmers: Hilda and Olaf, who run East Farm together, she in the farmhouse and he in the barn. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
army:"The island's army, based at the barracks. Colonel Halvorsen commands it from the Officers' HQ; under him Sergeant Rask, the quartermaster, keeps the armoury and the men: Corporal Niemi, the army cook, Private Aho in the barracks and Private Koski on sentry at the guard post. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
food:"The people who feed the island. On the streets: Dex and Rosa with their hot dog carts and Pirkko with her food van at the Kelp Cola factory. Indoors: Maya at the Coffee Roasters and Arvid at the Cedar Grill in Eastbrook, and Sanna at Polar Burger in Frostholm. It has no leader. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
shops:"The people who run the island's shops and stalls: in Kingsgrad Frank (guns), Jack (fishing gear), Mary (books), Lisa (the supermarket) and Grace (tailoring); in Eastbrook Juniper (clothes), Ruby (records) and Wilma (the Kelp Cola Museum's gift shop); in Frostholm Nils (electronics) and Birgit (Nordmart); in Saltwick Olga (fish); and the newsstand vendors Ville and Hannu. It has no leader. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
proprietors:"The people who run the island's businesses that are not shops: the bartenders Ray in Saltwick, Eddie at the City Bar and Linnea at the Timberline Tavern; Sid, who owns The Midnight Note; Otto at the cinema; Vince at the casino, Toni at the arcade and Greta at Hotel Aurora; Saga at the Hot Springs Spa; Sally the estate agent; and Jonna the tattoo artist. It has no leader. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
entertainers:"The island's performers: Leo and Rita, the saxophonist and singer at The Midnight Note; Kaisa, the DJ on Radio Sarivalto; and Jaana, who plays Kelpy the cup at the Kelp Cola Museum. (The circus performers at Lake Ilmari have their own group, the Circus.) It has no leader. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
admin:"The people who keep the island's paperwork in order: Bertil, a clerk at the Civil Service Bureau in Kingsgrad; Agnes, the teller at Nordbank in Frostholm, Ole, the harbourmaster at North Frostholm Harbour, who logs every boat in and out, and Signe, who keeps the lighthouse at Eastbrook Harbour. It has no leader. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
unemployed:"The island's people without work: Pat, a hobo who camps in a tent by the campfire on the beach, Sirpa and Tiina from Saltwick's apartment block, who hang about on the main street by day and sit in the bar in the evenings, Eila and Marjut from the Kingsgrad Apartments, who do the same by the bench at the west end of Kingsgrad and in the City Bar, Veikko and Hely from Eastbrook's Timber Lofts, by the bench in Eastbrook's square and in the Timberline Tavern, and Arto and Raili from Frostholm's Skyline Apartments, by the phone box on the boulevard and in The Midnight Note. It has no leader. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
police:"The island's police, run from Kingsgrad Police Station. For now it is just Sergeant Hanna, the desk sergeant, who keeps watch over the station's three cells, the island's jail, and its one prisoner, the Syndicate's bookie Mario. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
palace:"The staff of the Royal Palace. Edmund the butler runs the household, with Oskar the footman under him; Marta the cook runs the kitchen and the laundress, Elsa; Ingrid and Lotta are the maids, and Viktor keeps the grounds. Edmund, Oskar and Marta are royalists, loyal to the family they serve. In the evening the staff are spread around the palace: Edmund in the throne room, Oskar and Viktor in the Grand Hall, Marta serving in the dining room, Lotta in the kitchen, Ingrid in the library and Elsa along the royal apartments' corridor. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
reporters:"The press: the Eastbrook Gazette's editor, Henrik, and his reporter, Nora, who work from the paper's office in Eastbrook and keep it out of the island's politics. It is a group, not a faction: it plays its part in the story but cannot win it.",
church:"The northern Orthodox Church. Its monastery stands on a mountain top, where the monks live under their abbot, Father Thyme, and his prior, Brother Anselm. Down in Eastbrook it has two faithful members of its own: Pirkko, who runs the food van at the Kelp Cola factory, and Juniper, who owns the Flannel and Folk clothes shop. Its most powerful friend is Prince Augustus, the late king's devout son: the monastery wants him, not his brother Leopold, on the throne."},
npcs:{
tom:{work:'harbour',note:"A fisherman who works at West Saltwick Harbour and lives in his own house in Saltwick. He is a member of the Union."},
sam:{work:'harbour',note:"A fisherman and Communist Party member who works at West Saltwick Harbour and lives in his own house in Saltwick. He is a member of the Union."},
bob:{work:'plant',note:"A fishmonger who works in the fish processing plant beside Kate. He lives in the village's apartment block with his partner, Helen, a Communist Party member. Her comrades frown on it, since he won't join. He is a member of the Union."},
kate:{work:'plant',note:"A fishmonger and Communist Party member who works in the fish processing plant beside Bob, and lives in her own house in Saltwick. She is a member of the Union."},
anna:{work:'hq',note:"The leader of the Communist Party, who works at the party's headquarters in Saltwick and lives in the village's apartment block. She is also a member of the Union, which her comrade Helen leads."},
mike:{work:'harbour',note:"A fisherman and Communist Party member who works at West Saltwick Harbour and lives in the village's apartment block with his partner, Lucia, a Crime Syndicate enforcer. Neither the party nor the Syndicate knows, and neither would approve. He is a member of the Union."},
helen:{work:'hq',note:"A Communist Party member who leads the Union, the island's trade union, working from a desk at the party's headquarters in Saltwick. She lives in the village's apartment block with her partner, Bob, a fishmonger at the fish processing plant and one of the Union's members. The party frowns on it, since he won't join."},
arto:{work:'fishing',note:"Out of work, like his friend Raili. He lives in the Skyline Apartments, spends his days hanging about by the phone box at the west end of Frostholm's boulevard, and his evenings in The Midnight Note."},
raili:{work:'fishing',note:"Out of work, like her friend Arto. She lives in the Skyline Apartments, spends her days hanging about by the phone box at the west end of Frostholm's boulevard, and her evenings in The Midnight Note."},
signe:{work:'lighthouse_in',note:"The keeper of the lighthouse at Eastbrook Harbour, who lives in the keeper's room at the foot of the tower and keeps the lamp lit through the night. Her fishing boat is moored at the Eastbrook jetty."},
rosaria:{work:'pizzeria_in',note:"She runs the pizzeria in Kingsgrad, day and evening, and makes the island's best pizza. The pizzeria is a front for the Crime Syndicate, of which she is a member, and its back room is where the Syndicate counts its money. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
veikko:{work:'second',note:"Out of work, like his friend Hely. He lives in the Timber Lofts, spends his days hanging about by the bench in Eastbrook's square, and his evenings in the Timberline Tavern."},
hely:{work:'second',note:"Out of work, like her friend Veikko. She lives in the Timber Lofts, spends her days hanging about by the bench in Eastbrook's square, and her evenings in the Timberline Tavern."},
eila:{work:'town',note:"Out of work, like her friend Marjut. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments, spends her days hanging about by the bench at the west end of town, and her evenings in the City Bar."},
marjut:{work:'town',note:"Out of work, like her friend Eila. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments, spends her days hanging about by the bench at the west end of town, and her evenings in the City Bar."},
sirpa:{work:'village',note:"Out of work, like her friend Tiina. She lives in Saltwick's apartment block, spends her days hanging about by the bench on the main street, and her evenings in the bar."},
tiina:{work:'village',note:"Out of work, like her friend Sirpa. She lives in Saltwick's apartment block, spends her days hanging about by the bench on the main street, and her evenings in the bar."},
ray:{work:'bar',note:"The bartender at the village's bar, who lives in the flat above it."},
phil:{work:'kchq2',note:"The CEO of Kelp Cola. He works in his office on the second floor of the company's headquarters and lives in a villa in Hope Springs."},
leopold:{note:"The prince, heir of the late king. He lives in the Royal Palace with his brother and sister. His claim to the throne is not safe: the Orthodox Church would rather see his devout brother, Augustus, crowned."},
augustus:{note:"Prince Leopold's brother, who lives with him in the Royal Palace. He is deeply religious, a devoted member of the Orthodox Church, and the monastery backs him to be king in place of his brother."},
'father-thyme':{work:'monastery',note:"The abbot of the Mountain-Top Monastery, who leads the Orthodox Church and its monks. He lives in his own house in the monastery's grounds."},
'brother-anselm':{work:'monastery',note:"The prior of the Mountain-Top Monastery, second to the abbot, Father Thyme, and in charge of the monks' daily life. He lives with them in the Monks' Quarters."},
'brother-paavo':{work:'monastery',note:"A monk who tends the monastery's kitchen garden, even under the snow."},
'brother-ilja':{work:'monks',note:"A monk and scribe, who copies books at the writing desk in the refectory of the Monks' Quarters."},
'brother-teodor':{work:'monks',note:"A monk who cooks for the brothers in the kitchen of the Monks' Quarters."},
'brother-mikael':{note:"The oldest monk at the Mountain-Top Monastery."},
daphne:{note:"Prince Leopold's sister, who lives with him in the Royal Palace."},
dario:{work:'oilhq',note:"The CEO of Diversified Petroleum. He works at the company's headquarters and lives in a villa in Hope Springs."},
gustavo:{work:'clubroom',note:"The Don of the Crime Syndicate. He lives in a villa in Hope Springs and holds court at his table in The Club."},
chuck:{note:"Your CIA handler. He works from an office upstairs at CIA Headquarters in Langley, behind the big desk, where he briefs you before you leave. He is not on the island: once you are there, the only way to reach him is over the radio in Hekki's Shack."},
hekki:{note:"A radio technician who looks after the Radio Tower and, in secret, an informant for the CIA. He lives in a shack near the tower. His radio set is the only way to reach Chuck, your handler. Behind a bookcase in his shack is a hidden room full of listening equipment."},
frank:{work:'gunshop',note:"Frank runs the gun shop in Kingsgrad and lives in a house in the city. He is a member of the Republican Party."},
lisa:{work:'supermarket',note:"Lisa works on the checkout at the Kingsgrad supermarket, which stays open into the evening, and lives in a house in the city."},
eddie:{work:'citybar',note:"Eddie is the bartender at the City Bar in Kingsgrad and lives in a house in the city."},
grace:{work:'tailor',note:"Grace is Kingsgrad's tailor. She lives in a house in the city."},
vince:{work:'casino',note:"Vince works at the casino in Frostholm and lives in a house in Kingsgrad."},
mary:{work:'bookshop',note:"Mary runs the book shop in Kingsgrad and lives in a house in the city."},
jack:{work:'fishingshop',note:"Jack runs the fishing shop in Kingsgrad and lives in a house in the city. He is a member of the Republican Party."},
sally:{work:'estateagent',note:"Sally is Kingsgrad's estate agent. She lives in a house in the city."},
pat:{note:"A hobo who camps on the beach."},
edmund:{work:'palacehall',note:"The royal family's butler, who runs the palace household. He lives in the servants' quarters."},
oskar:{work:'palace',note:"A footman in the royal livery who keeps the palace door. He lives in the servants' quarters."},
marta:{work:'kitchen',note:"The palace cook, who runs the palace kitchen. She lives in the servants' quarters."},
ingrid:{work:'royalrooms',note:"A maid who looks after the royal bedrooms. She lives in the servants' quarters."},
lotta:{work:'dining',note:"A maid who serves in the palace dining room. She lives in the servants' quarters."},
viktor:{work:'palace',note:"The palace groundskeeper, who clears the snow and keeps the formal garden. He lives in the servants' quarters."},
pirkko:{work:'colafactory',note:"Pirkko runs the HOT FOOD van parked outside the Kelp Cola factory, feeding the factory workers burgers, hot dogs, coffee and cola. She lives in a house in Eastbrook, takes the tram to work, and is a member of the Orthodox Church."},
kaisa:{work:'transhut',note:"The island's radio DJ, who presents the shows from the studio in the transmitter hut by the Radio Tower. She lives in the apartment block in Saltwick."},
henrik:{work:'newsroom',note:"The editor of the Eastbrook Gazette, the town's newspaper. He lives in a house across the street from the office, and keeps the paper out of the island's politics: he belongs to no party."},
nora:{work:'newsroom',note:"A reporter on the Eastbrook Gazette. She lives a few doors from her editor, Henrik, in Eastbrook, and like him belongs to no party."},
olga:{work:'fishshop',note:"She runs Saltwick's fish shop and lives in the village's apartment block."},
helmi:{work:'outfitters_in',note:"She runs Harbour Outfitters in Saltwick, kitting out the island's fishermen in oilskins and knitwear, and lives in the village's apartment block. She can tell what a man does for a living from the state of his boots."},
nils:{work:'electro',note:"He runs the electronics store in Frostholm, lives in the Skyline Apartments and is a member of the Republican Party."},
toni:{work:'arcadein',note:"The attendant at Frostholm's arcade. Toni lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
birgit:{work:'mart',note:"She manages the Nordmart store in Frostholm and lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
otto:{work:'cinemain',note:"He manages Kingsgrad's cinema, which shows films into the evening, lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments and is a member of the Republican Party."},
sanna:{work:'burgerbar',note:"The cook at Polar Burger in Frostholm. She lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
maya:{work:'cafe',note:"She roasts the coffee at Eastbrook's coffee roaster, lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party."},
jonna:{work:'tattoo',note:"She runs Eastbrook's tattoo shop, lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party."},
linnea:{work:'tavern',note:"The bartender at the Timberline Tavern in Eastbrook. She lives in the Timber Lofts and is a royalist, loyal to the Royal Family."},
arvid:{work:'cedargrill',note:"The chef at the Cedar Grill in Eastbrook. He lives in the Timber Lofts and is a royalist, loyal to the Royal Family."},
ville:{work:'colahq',note:"He runs the newsstand outside Kelp Cola HQ and lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
rosa:{work:'colahq',note:"She runs the hot dog cart outside Kelp Cola HQ and lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
'doctor-lind':{work:'doctor',note:"Kingsgrad's doctor, who works at the doctor's office below the police station and lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments. He works evenings too, on call through the night. He is a member of the Republican Party."},
yuri:{work:'hotel_floor',note:"A KGB agent, posing as a businessman, who lives in a room at Hotel Aurora in Frostholm. He has fitted it out with his own radio equipment, screens and tape recorder to listen in on the island, much as you do. He works with the Communist Party as the Soviet Union's man on the island."},
greta:{work:'hotel_lobby',note:"The receptionist at Hotel Aurora in Frostholm. She lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
'lars':{work:'crewq',note:"A roughneck on Diversified Petroleum's oil rig, who lives in the rig's crew quarters."},
'einar':{work:'oilrig',note:"A roughneck on Diversified Petroleum's oil rig, working the deck beside the drill tower. He lives in the rig's crew quarters with Lars."},
'ruth':{work:'dphq_in',note:"The receptionist at Diversified Petroleum's headquarters. She lives in the Skyline Apartments in Frostholm."},
'britta':{work:'depot_in',note:"She looks after Diversified Petroleum's depot and lives in the Skyline Apartments in Frostholm."},
'mats':{work:'petro_in',note:"A clerk in Diversified Petroleum's offices in the Petro Tower. He lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments with his partner, Elin, Phil's secretary at the rival Kelp Cola. Neither company knows: with both trying to win the Republican Party's leadership, either of them could be passing on secrets."},
'agnes':{work:'bank_in',note:"A teller at Nordbank in Frostholm. She lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
'hilda':{work:'farmhouse_in',note:"She runs East Farm with her husband, Olaf, and they live in the farmhouse."},
'olaf':{work:'barn_in',note:"He runs East Farm with his wife, Hilda, working in the barn, and they live in the farmhouse."},
'bertil':{work:'civil_in',note:"A clerk at the Civil Service Bureau in Kingsgrad. He lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
'elin':{work:'kchq_in',note:"Phil's secretary at Kelp Cola's headquarters. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments with her partner, Mats, a clerk at Kelp Cola's rival, Diversified Petroleum. Neither company knows: with both trying to win the Republican Party's leadership, either of them could be passing on secrets."},
'kurt':{work:'kcfac_in',note:"The foreman on the bottling line at the Kelp Cola factory. He lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
'petra':{work:'kcwhs_in',note:"She works in Kelp Cola's warehouse and lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments. She is a member of the Union."},
'aino':{work:'kcfac_in',note:"She works the bottling line on the Kelp Cola factory floor, under the foreman, Kurt. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments, takes the tram to work, and is a member of the Union."},
'gunnar':{work:'whs_in',note:"He works in the warehouse at West Saltwick Harbour and lives in the village's apartment block. He is a member of the Union."},
'private-aho':{work:'barrA_in',note:"A soldier at the Army Barracks, who sleeps in the dormitory of Block A."},
'corporal-niemi':{work:'barrB_in',note:"The cook in the barracks mess hall. He sleeps in Block A with the other soldiers."},
'private-koski':{work:'gp_in',note:"The sentry on duty at the barracks guard post. He sleeps in Block A."},
'sergeant-rask':{work:'arm_in',note:"The quartermaster in charge of the barracks armoury. He sleeps in Block A."},
'colonel-halvorsen':{work:'offhq_in',note:"The commander of the island's army, who works from the Officers' HQ at the barracks and lives in the Hope Springs Residences."},
'sven':{work:'fuel_in',note:"He runs the fuel dock at North Frostholm Harbour for Diversified Petroleum, and lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
'ole':{work:'port_in',note:"The harbourmaster at North Frostholm Harbour, who logs every boat in and out. He lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
'liv':{work:'customs_in',note:"The customs officer at Eastbrook Harbour. She lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Communist Party, unusual in Democratic Eastbrook."},
'tor':{work:'ebwhs_in',note:"He runs the timber warehouse at Eastbrook Harbour, lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Communist Party, unusual in Democratic Eastbrook."},
bruno:{work:'lake',note:"The ringmaster of the travelling circus camped at Lake Ilmari. He lives in the ringmaster's caravan."},
buttons:{work:'lake',note:"The circus jester, in cap and motley, who juggles and tells jokes for visitors by the campfire at Lake Ilmari. He lives in the performers' caravan with his partner, Meg the acrobat."},
meg:{work:'bigtop_in',note:"The circus acrobat, who rehearses in the big top. She lives in the performers' caravan with her partner, Buttons the jester."},
igor:{work:'bigtop_in',note:"The circus strongman. He shares the ringmaster's caravan with Bruno."},
'madame-zora':{work:'caravan3_in',note:"The circus fortune teller, who reads fortunes in her own caravan at Lake Ilmari."},
nico:{note:"A bookie for the Crime Syndicate, who takes bets and collects debts in Frostholm. He lives in the Skyline Apartments in Frostholm."},
paolo:{note:"A bookie for the Crime Syndicate, who takes bets and collects debts in Eastbrook. He lives in the Timber Lofts in Eastbrook."},
mario:{work:'police',note:"A bookie for the Crime Syndicate, who took bets and collected debts in Kingsgrad until he was arrested. He is locked in the middle cell of Kingsgrad Police Station, day and night; you can talk to him through the bars."},
lucia:{note:"An enforcer for the Crime Syndicate, who makes sure people in Saltwick pay what they owe. She lives in the apartment block in Saltwick with her partner, Mike, a Communist fisherman. Neither the Syndicate nor the party knows, and neither would approve."},
paola:{note:"An enforcer for the Crime Syndicate, who makes sure people in Hope Springs Gated Community pay what they owe. She lives in the Hope Springs Residences."},
jaana:{work:'kcmuseum_in',note:"The woman inside Kelpy, the Kelp Cola Museum's mascot: a giant cola cup with a striped straw, white gloves and big shoes. All day she stands on Eastbrook's main street outside the museum, waving visitors in. She lives in the Timber Lofts."},
hannu:{work:'village',note:"He runs the newsstand on Saltwick's main street, as worn as everything else in the village, and lives in the village's apartment block."},
sid:{work:'jazz_in',note:"He owns The Midnight Note, Frostholm's jazz club, and tends its bar. He lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
leo:{work:'jazz_in',note:"The saxophonist at The Midnight Note, Frostholm's jazz club. He lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
rita:{work:'jazz_in',note:"The singer at The Midnight Note, Frostholm's jazz club. She lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
erik:{work:'commcentre',note:"The leader of the Democratic Party, who runs it from Eastbrook's Community Centre. He lives in the Timber Lofts."},
margit:{work:'repubhq',note:"The Republican Party's secretary, who runs the election for its new leader at the party HQ in Frostholm. She lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
harald:{work:'kchq_in',note:"A Kelp Cola executive, and the company's candidate for leader of the Republican Party. He works at Kelp Cola's headquarters, campaigning from there rather than from the party HQ in Frostholm, and lives in the Hope Springs Residences."},
magnus:{work:'dphq_in',note:"A Diversified Petroleum executive, and the company's candidate for leader of the Republican Party. He works at Diversified Petroleum's headquarters, campaigning from there rather than from the party HQ in Frostholm, and lives in the Skyline Apartments."},
carlo:{work:'repubhq',note:"The Crime Syndicate's candidate for leader of the Republican Party, campaigning from the party HQ in Frostholm. He lives in the Hope Springs Residences."},
dex:{work:'second',note:"He runs the hot dog cart on Eastbrook's food-cart plaza, which he calls The Dogfather. He lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party."},
wilma:{work:'kcmuseum_in',note:"The curator of the Kelp Cola Museum in Eastbrook, who also runs its gift shop. She works for Kelp Cola and lives in the Timber Lofts."},
juniper:{work:'clothes_in',note:"She owns Flannel and Folk, Eastbrook's vintage clothes shop. She lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Orthodox Church."},
ruby:{work:'records_in',note:"She owns Vinyl Resting Place, Eastbrook's record shop. She lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party."},
bjarne:{work:'mill_in',note:"The foreman of the Eastbrook Lumber Company's mill, at the Mill. He lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party."},
knut:{work:'mill_in',note:"The sawyer at the lumber mill, who runs the big circular saw. He lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party. He is a member of the Union."},
ilse:{work:'millroad',note:"She loads logs in the lumber mill's yard, at the Mill. She lives in the Timber Lofts and is a member of the Democratic Party. She is a member of the Union."},
saga:{work:'spa_in',note:"The attendant at the Hot Springs Spa on the volcano's lower slopes, who runs the front desk and hands out towels. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
'sergeant-hanna':{work:'police',note:"The desk sergeant at Kingsgrad Police Station, who keeps watch over the cells, evenings included. She lives in the Kingsgrad Apartments."},
elsa:{work:'servants',note:"The palace laundress, who washes for the whole household in the servants' quarters, where she lives."}}};
